From: lighter <build@invalid>
Subject: virtio_balloon: free page reporting at four host pages

Free page reporting reports free runs of the pageblock order, 2 MiB, by
default. The host releases 16 KiB pages, so any aligned run of four is worth
reporting. lighter's agent sets the order itself once it runs (128 KiB at
rest, the pageblock order while containers churn); this is the kernel's own
default for the moments before it speaks, and for a guest without it. The
driver registers with an order of 4 (64 KiB); the core honours the driver's
order when the `page_reporting_order` parameter is unset.

---
--- a/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
+++ b/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
@@ -1119,6 +1119,13 @@
 #if defined(CONFIG_ARM64) && defined(CONFIG_ARM64_64K_PAGES)
 		vb->pr_dev_info.order = 5;
 #endif
+		/* lighter: report at four host pages, 64 KiB, not a 2 MiB
+		 * pageblock. The host releases 16 KiB pages, so a run of four
+		 * is worth reporting, and a guest that has run containers for
+		 * days has few whole pageblocks free: at the pageblock order
+		 * it reported almost nothing of what it freed.
+		 */
+		vb->pr_dev_info.order = 4;
 
 		err = page_reporting_register(&vb->pr_dev_info);
 		if (err)
